* The empty interface

The interface type that specifies zero methods is known as the ⟪GTI18N_f85eea0b_000001⟫empty_interface⟪GTI18N_f85eea0b_000002⟫:

⟪GTI18N_f85eea0b_000003⟫

An empty interface may hold values of any type.
(Every type implements at least zero methods.)

Empty interfaces are used by code that handles values of unknown type.
For example, ⟪GTI18N_f85eea0b_000004⟫fmt.Print⟪GTI18N_f85eea0b_000005⟫ takes any number of arguments of type ⟪GTI18N_f85eea0b_000006⟫interface{}⟪GTI18N_f85eea0b_000007⟫.

